# DIP

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Dip is a bodyweight compound pushing exercise performed by lowering and raising the body between parallel bars.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the foundational exercises for developing upper-body relative strength, pressing power and shoulder stability.

---

# Philosophy

The Dip combines pressing strength with body control.

Unlike machine-based pressing exercises, the athlete must stabilize the entire body while producing force.

CAS selects the Dip when developing relative pushing strength and shoulder robustness.

